  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Prashant Agrawal vs Deputy Director on 6 January, 2016 1 Cr.R.No.279/2010 High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Bench At Gwalior Sb: Justice N.K. Gupta Cr.R. No. 279/2010 Prashant Agrawal and Another Vs. Deputy Director, Food and Drug Administration and Anr",
    "facts": "The applicants have challenged the order dated 04/02/2010 passed by Judicial Magistrate First Class, Gwalior in Criminal Case No. 6196/2006, whereby, charges of offence under section 16(1)(a)(1) of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act (in short \"PF Act\") were framed against the applicants. 2. The facts of the case in short are that the applicants were found selling some Papad, etc. The Food Inspector found that the Papad sold by the applicants were adulterated and misbranded and, therefore, a complaint was filed. 3. After hearing submissions made by learned counsel for the parties, the Judicial Magistrate First Class has passed the impugned order dated 04/02/2010 and charges were framed.",
    "arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the applicants has also submitted that the sample could not be said to be misbranded in the light of judgment passed by Punjab and Haryana High Court in the case of Om Prakash vs. State of Punjab reported in 2000 (2) FAC 253.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the applicants has also submitted that the sample could not be said to be misbranded in the light of judgment passed by Punjab and Haryana High Court in the case of Om Prakash vs. State of Punjab reported in 2000 (2) FAC 253.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
